--[[
Every item of the game: weapons, armor, charms, consumables, materials and artefacts.

- Weapons go in the active slot. Melee weapons hit in front of the player (`reach` in tiles),
  ranged ones shoot a projectile (`shot`) and use ammunition (`ammo`) or sanity (`sanityCost`).
- Armor reduces damage (`defense`), more against some damage types (`resist`, a multiplier of the damage taken).
- Charms go in one of the two charm slots and give a bonus: `light` (radius), `luck` (more drops), `regen` (health per second).
  The bonuses of the two charms add up.
- Bombs (`bomb`) are equipped like weapons: each attack drops one of them, lit (see combat.luau).
- Consumables are used from the bag: `heal`, `water`, `sanity`, `cure` (removes poison), `bottle` (more sips
  in the water bottle, for good).
- Artefacts are unique powers of the sea people. Once found, they are always active and listed in the notebook.

`requires` is the minimum stats needed to equip an item. `value` is what traders give or ask for it, in figs.
Damage types: blunt, slash, pierce, fire, electric, acid, cold, dream (see data/monsters.luau for weaknesses).

The frontier: `dreamOnly` weapons only work while the player dreams (see dream.luau). Cold weapons slow down the
creatures they hit (see combat.luau). Armor with `warm` keeps that fraction of the cold (see frost.luau), charms
with a `warm` bonus keep the cold away too. `use.dream` sinks the player into the dream, `use.warmth` warms them up.
]]
const loader = require("@vectarine/loader")
const types = require("../types")

export type ItemKind = "weapon" | "armor" | "charm" | "consumable" | "material" | "artefact"

export type Item = {
	name: string,
	icon: string,
	kind: ItemKind,
	description: string,
	--- How many fit in one slot of the bag (1 when not set)
	stack: number?,
	damage: number?,
	damageType: types.DamageType?,
	reach: number?,
	--- Seconds between two attacks
	cooldown: number?,
	shot: string?,
	ammo: string?,
	sanityCost: number?,
	bomb: boolean?,
	dreamOnly: boolean?,
	--- Weapons that light the way (a torch): added to the light around the player
	light: number?,
	warm: number?,
	defense: number?,
	resist: { [types.DamageType]: number }?,
	bonus: { light: number?, luck: number?, regen: number?, warm: number?, insulate: number?, speed: number? }?,
	requires: { [types.StatName]: number }?,
	use: {
		heal: number?,
		water: number?,
		sanity: number?,
		cure: boolean?,
		bottle: number?,
		dream: boolean?,
		warmth: number?,
		--- A temporary buff (see player.BUFFS), for `seconds`
		buff: string?,
		seconds: number?,
	}?,
	value: number?,
}

